# Google is this codebase's style already: 2-space indent, left-attached
# references (`const T& x` outnumbers `const T &x` here 937 to 1), and Google's
# brace and wrapping rules. Two things are changed.
#
# ColumnLimit 100, not Google's 80. The code sits at p50=40, p90=78, p99=95, so
# 80 would reflow the top tenth of every file for no gain while 100 covers all
# but a short tail. A formatter that rewrites code nobody is editing buries
# real diffs, which is the one thing it must not do.
#
# AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine, because the switches that map an enum to
# its name are written as TABLES -- one case per line, case and result side by
# side -- and Google's default breaks each into two lines, turning a readable
# table into a column. That is a deliberate style, so the formatter yields.
BasedOnStyle: Google
ColumnLimit: 100
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: true
